# Document Sync

Before writing or analyzing code/tests, read `Document/00-AI/CONTEXT.md` (then Glossary / related Architecture or Reference notes).

When you change `Source/`, `Test/`, `Sandbox/`, `Examples/`, or `TemplateSource/`, update `Document/` in the **same turn**.

## Map changes to notes

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| Public API / contracts | `03-Reference/Public-API.md` |
| Packages / projects | `03-Reference/Packages.md`, `02-Architecture/Components.md` |
| Folder or project layout | `02-Architecture/Overview.md`, `Components.md`, `01-Overview/Scope.md` |
| Runtime behavior / flow | `02-Architecture/Data-Flow.md` |
| New architectural choice | `05-Decisions/NNNN-*.md` (from `_Template.md`) |
| Bugs / pitfalls | `06-Troubleshooting/FAQ.md` |
| How to use | `04-Guides/` |

## Rules

- Prefer facts from code over speculation; do not invent docs without code evidence.
- When replacing stubs, set `status` and `updated` in frontmatter; add one line to `_meta/Changelog.md`.
- Keep Obsidian `[[WikiLink]]` and vault conventions (`Document/00-AI/CONVENTIONS.md`).
- Do not refactor Document for style alone; sync only what the code change requires.
- Follow skill `ds-document-vault` for the full checklist.